;; ci: calls (doc/c/SPEC.md §7.6, §13.3): the arguments evaluated right to left as gcc 15.2's -O0
;; code does on x86-64 (CS31 (a)), passed as Args; a static call holds the callee's cell, so a
;; redefinition at the REPL is seen; a call through a pointer finds the function by its address.
(in-ns 'go.arbace.ci) (go/file "call.go" :doc "ci: calls (doc/c/SPEC.md §7.6, §13.3): the arguments evaluated right to left as gcc 15.2's -O0\ncode does on x86-64 (CS31 (a)), passed as Args; a static call holds the callee's cell, so a\nredefinition at the REPL is seen; a call through a pointer finds the function by its address.\n" :imports [

    ^{:line 6} [crt "arbace/crt"]])

